# Monday DSA Plan (Interview Focus)

## Goal

Complete the remaining Two Pointer topic and establish a solid foundation in Binary Search.

Duration: **2.5–3 Hours**

---

# Session 1 (45–60 Minutes)

## 1. Trapping Rain Water ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Concepts

- Brute Force
- Prefix Max Array
- Suffix Max Array
- Two Pointer Optimization
- Why Two Pointers Work

Interview Focus

- Derive the optimized solution from the brute-force approach.
- Explain the intuition instead of memorizing the code.

---

# Session 2 (30 Minutes)

## Binary Search Fundamentals

Topics

- When Binary Search is applicable
- Loop Invariants
- Mid Calculation
- Left / Right Pointer Movement
- Common Mistakes
- Time Complexity

Practice

- Binary Search (LeetCode 704)

---

# Session 3 (45 Minutes)

## Search in Rotated Sorted Array ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Concepts

- Why Binary Search still works
- Identifying the sorted half
- Deciding which half to discard

Interview Focus

Many product companies ask this problem or a variation of it.

---

# Session 4 (30 Minutes)

## Find Minimum in Rotated Sorted Array

Concepts

- Binary Search on rotated arrays
- Comparing middle with right
- Why the minimum always lies in one half

---

# Session 5 (30 Minutes)

## Koko Eating Bananas

Concepts

- Binary Search on the Answer
- Search Space
- Feasibility Function

Interview Focus

This introduces the important "Binary Search on Answer" pattern.

---

# Revision (15–20 Minutes)

Revise:

## Arrays & Hashing

- Two Sum
- Group Anagrams
- Product Except Self
- Longest Consecutive Sequence
- Top K Frequent Elements

---

## Sliding Window

